# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v1.0.18)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `src/App.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the App's JSX return statement (after Footer component)

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart):
- Used the React-specific export path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Placed the component at the root level of the app for proper tracking across all pages
- The component is self-contained and requires no additional configuration

## Verification

✅ **Build**: Successfully compiled with `npm run build` - no errors
✅ **Linter**: Passed with 0 warnings and 0 errors using oxlint
✅ **Tests**: No test script available (skipped)
✅ **Lock files**: package-lock.json updated with new dependencies

## Next Steps for Deployment

To start collecting Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Speed Insights section)
3. After deployment, metrics will begin appearing in the dashboard (data typically appears after a few days of user traffic)

Note: Speed Insights is available on all Vercel plans and will only track metrics once deployed to Vercel's platform.
